      "id": 100,
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Hubble Live Topology\n\nEvery pod-to-pod conversation currently flowing through this cluster, decoded by the Cilium eBPF datapath at the moment each packet crosses the network namespace boundary. Refreshes every 5 seconds.\n\n**Nodes** are workloads (deployment / statefulset / daemonset names). **Edges** are flow rates between them over the last 5 minutes. Edge thickness encodes traffic volume. Verdict (FORWARDED, DROPPED, ERROR) decomposes into separate edges so a policy drop appears as its own line, not merged into the forwarded total.\n\n**EQUIVALENT IN OTHER TOOLS.** Splunk Stream, Loki host-exporter, and Dynatrace agent panels render flow data as tables or time-series lists. None decode pod identity at the kernel boundary; identity in those products is application-layer (the app reports who it is). Cilium reads it from the BPF datapath's per-endpoint identity map, which is set when the pod's network namespace is created and is unforgeable from inside the pod.\n\nThe table panel below is the same data in tabular form — useful when the topology graph has too many nodes to read at a glance."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 110,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Live cluster topology",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 6 },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 111,
      "type": "nodeGraph",
      "title": "Service topology — live pod-to-pod flows",
      "gridPos": { "h": 16, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 7 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "edges",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "topk(80, sum by (source, destination) (rate(hubble_flows_processed_total{source!=\"\",destination!=\"\",verdict=\"FORWARDED\"}[5m])))",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": { "Time": true },
            "indexByName": {},
            "renameByName": { "Value": "mainstat" }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "calculateField",
          "options": {
            "mode": "binary",
            "binary": { "left": "source", "operator": "+", "right": "destination" },
            "reduce": { "reducer": "sum" },
            "alias": "id",
            "replaceFields": false
          }
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "nodes": {
          "mainStatUnit": "reqps"
        },
        "edges": {
          "mainStatUnit": "reqps"
        }
      },
      "description": "Live cluster topology decoded from the Cilium BPF datapath via hubble_flows_processed_total. One edge per src/dst workload pair; thickness = forwarded-flow rate over the last 5 minutes. To produce drops as separate edges, change the query verdict filter from FORWARDED to DROPPED, or remove the filter to combine."
    },
    {
      "id": 120,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Same data, tabular",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 23 },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 121,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Top 50 edges — workload to workload (by flow rate)",
